Package: rsageIntegrity
Title: Data Integrity Check Module for R Sage
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("R Sage contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "noreply@rsage.dev")
Description: Checks a data frame received as a spreadsheet before analysis:
    column names, empty rows and columns, numbers stored as text, mixed date
    formats, lost leading zeros, outliers, range, allowed-value and order
    rules, hidden missing-value codes, duplicate rows and keys, whitespace
    and spelling variants in text. Variable diagnosis, outlier statistics
    and the HTML diagnosis report use 'dlookr'; the other checks are the
    module's own. It can also return a cleaned copy of the data.
    analyse() returns an 'rsage' result that prints in the console and
    renders in Quarto documents.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: rsage (>= 0.1.0), dlookr (>= 0.6.0), tibble, ggplot2, stats, utils
Suggests: stringi, rmarkdown, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
